# Garbage
*.*_2DEL
*.log
m

# Linux complained part
sys/lib/ape/locale.alias
sys/src/ape/cmd/**/lib*.a[01256789kqtv]
sys/src/cmd/*c/enam.c
sys/src/external/f2c/lib/arithchk

# vts's host test binaries, built by sys/src/cmd2/vts/test/run_tests.sh
sys/src/cmd2/vts/test/bin/

# Claude Code harness artifacts
.claude/

# cfront's leftovers. CFRONT IS REMOVED FROM THE TREE -- `cmd/cfront',
# `cmd/c++lib' and `cfrontsz-probe' are gone, and `external/cfront-C4'
# holds nothing tracked. This line stays because a checkout that ever
# built c++lib still has the 40 generated `.c' on disk, untracked: they
# were once COMMITTED AT ZERO BYTES, so a fresh checkout compiled 40
# empty translation units into `libc++.a' and the build reported success
# -- a check that cannot fail. Keeping the line costs nothing and means
# `git status' in such a checkout is readable.
sys/src/ape/cmd/c++lib/*.c

# THE RULE cfrontsz-probe PAID FOR, kept because the probe is gone and
# the rule is not: git IS the only channel to the VM, so an ignored
# GENERATED file is a file the VM never sees -- `pcc ... cfrontsz-probe.c'
# answered `Can't open input file' for exactly that reason. A generated
# file that something on the VM must READ gets committed. (Distinct from
# the c++lib case above, where the generated files were an INPUT to mk,
# which therefore never regenerated them.)

# cpfe/eccp template-instantiation request files (EDG prelink).
# Written beside the cwd by every cpfe run, VM and host alike.
*.ti

# eccp's intermediate C, one per translated .cpp (kept only with -K).
*.eccp.c

# Python bytecode. `bitinit-model.py' imports `sualign-model.py' by path,
# which makes CPython write a __pycache__ beside them.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# host builds of kencc (sys/lib/tests/hostkencc) -- binaries and objects
sys/lib/tests/hostkencc/out/

# go1.4's build output. `GOROOT_FINAL' is the SOURCE TREE
# (`sys/src/external/go1.4'), so the tools, the std archives and the
# finished `go' are all written inside it: `pkg/tool/plan9_$GOARCH' by
# `go-dist bootstrap', `pkg/plan9_$GOARCH' by `go_bootstrap install
# std', and `bin/go' by `install cmd/go'. None of it is
# pre-installable -- every file is a compiled archive or a binary, and
# both are architecture-specific.
sys/src/external/go1.4/pkg/
sys/src/external/go1.4/bin/

# clisp's build directory, one per architecture. It holds the 31
# generated `.c', `lisp.run', the three `.mem' images and ~90 `.fas'.
# **The base image cannot be pre-installed**: it is what the
# three-stage Lisp bootstrap produces. The only clisp files anything
# reads at runtime that are NOT build output are the two data files,
# and both are already tracked as source --
# `utils/unicode/UnicodeDataFull.txt' and `doc/Symbol-Table.text'.
sys/src/ape/cmd/clisp/build-*/

# munmaptrim-xcheck's generated extract and its host binary
sys/lib/tests/munmaptrim-extract.h
sys/lib/tests/munmaptrim-xcheck
